course: dictionary
lesson: 13443
title: Hospitable: friendly and welcoming
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hospitable is a word about kindness. It describes a person who is friendly and welcoming to guests and visitors. «The Hendersons were so hospitable that we felt at home the moment we arrived.» The clue is felt at home: they made us feel welcome, so hospitable means welcoming.
explain: Hospitable can also describe a place. «The island was hospitable, with fresh water, warm sunshine and plenty of food.» The clues are water, warmth and food, which are the things living things need. So a hospitable place is pleasant and easy to live in.
explain: The opposite is inhospitable. «The Moon is inhospitable: there is no air or water for living things.» The prefix in- often means not, so inhospitable means not welcoming, or not able to support life.
fact: Hospitable means friendly and welcoming to guests and visitors.
fact: Hospitable can also describe a place that is pleasant and easy to live in.
fact: «A hospitable climate» is a climate with water, warmth and food, so living things can survive there.
fact: Inhospitable is the opposite: a desert or the Moon is inhospitable.
fact: Hospitable is often used with «to», as in hospitable to visitors.
exercise: «The hospitable farmer gave us a hot dinner and a warm bed.» What does hospitable mean? | Very tall and thin | Angry and loud with visitors | *Friendly and welcoming to guests | Rich and famous
exercise: «The island was hospitable, with fresh water and plenty of food.» Which clue shows the island could support living things? | Its tall, grey cliffs | *Fresh water and plenty of food | Its loud, noisy waves at night | Its wooden boats on the beach
exercise: Which word means the opposite of hospitable? | Welcoming | Warm | *Inhospitable | Friendly
test: «The desert is inhospitable, with no water and no food.» What does inhospitable mean here? | Welcoming to guests | Full of trees and streams | *Not able to support life, and not welcoming | Very cold and snowy all year
test: Which sentence uses hospitable correctly? | «The Moon is hospitable, with lovely air and water.» | *«The hospitable hosts gave us a warm welcome.» | «The hospitable rain fell all day long.» | «The hospitable rock was grey and hard.»
exam: What does «a hospitable climate» mean? | A climate that is always freezing and empty | *A climate with water, warmth and food, so living things can survive | A climate that is loud and windy all day | A climate where nobody ever visits
